<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Oct consumer prices down 0.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Oct consumer prices down 0.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in the Tokyo area in October fell 0.1 percent from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices in September were unchanged from a year before, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				    OCT	  SEPT	  AUG</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	100.0	100.0	 99.8</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    -0.1 pct   -0.4 pct    0.0 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	   0.0 pct   +0.2 pct   -0.2 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	   100.1	100.0	 99.7</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    -0.1 pct   -0.3 pct    0.0 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  +0.1 pct   +0.3 pct   -0.2 pct</p>
<p>				  SEPT	 AUG	  JULY</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index 100.4	100.0	100.1</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	     0.0 pct   +0.2 pct   +0.4 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  +0.4 pct   -0.1 pct   -0.1 pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index    100.4	 99.9	100.1</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr change	    +0.2 pct   +0.2 pct   +0.3 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth change	  +0.5 pct   -0.2 pct   -0.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Tokyo index calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. Core indices are overall prices minus fresh food prices.</p>
<p>An agency official told a media briefing that Tokyo prices were on a stable trend on both a year-on-year and month-on-month basis.</p>
</text>
